2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
“approved entry levy collection system” means an entry levy collection system where all the specified parts of the entry levy collection system are approved by the Authority under regulation 9, 10 or 11, as the case may be;
[S 637/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“authorised person” means an authorised person appointed for the purposes of section 117 of the Act;
[S 637/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“Board” means the Singapore Totalisator Board established under the Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987;
[S 637/2026 wef 31/12/2021]
“entry levy” means the entry levy referred to in section 116(1) of the Act;
“entry levy collection requirements” has the meaning ascribed to it in regulation 7(1);
[S 637/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“entry levy collection system” means a system for the collection of the entry levy;
[S 637/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“law enforcement agency” has the meaning ascribed to it in section 186(6) of the Act;
[S 54/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
“Patron Dispute Committee” has the meaning ascribed to it in regulation 2 of the Casino Control (Patron Dispute Resolution) Regulations 2009 (G.N. No. S 432/2009);
[S 54/2013 wef 31/01/2013]
“resident” means a citizen of Singapore or a permanent resident of Singapore;
[S 637/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“specified parts of the entry levy collection system”, in relation to a casino operator or an applicant for a casino licence, means —
(a)the parts of the entry levy collection system specified by the Authority by notice in writing given to the casino operator or applicant, in respect of which the Authority’s approval is required under regulation 9, 10 or 11; or
(b)in the absence of any notice mentioned in paragraph (a), all parts of the entry levy collection system;
[S 637/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
“validity period”, in relation to an entry levy paid by a resident to a casino operator, means —
(a)in the case of an entry levy referred to in section 116(1)(a) of the Act, a consecutive period of 24 hours during which the resident may enter the casino premises of the casino operator; and
(b)in the case of an entry levy referred to in section 116(1)(b) of the Act, a consecutive period of 12 months during which the resident may enter the casino premises of the casino operator.

3. A resident wishing to enter the casino premises of a casino operator shall pay the appropriate entry levy by any of the following modes of payment which are accepted by the casino operator:
(a)in cash, cashier’s order or money order;
(b)by charging the entry levy to a debit card or credit card accepted by the casino operator;
(c)by an electronic funds transfer to the casino operator’s bank account;
(d)by the transfer of e-money (within the meaning given by the Payment Services Act 2019) to the casino operator’s payment account (within the meaning given by that Act).
[S 60/2020 wef 28/01/2020]
[S 637/2026 wef 31/12/2021]

9.—(1) A casino operator or an applicant for a casino licence, in its application for approval of the specified parts of its entry levy collection system, must include details of the following:
(a)a description of the specified parts of the entry levy collection system and how they meet the entry levy collection requirements and comply with any direction given by the Authority in relation to the collection of entry levy and with these Regulations;
(b)detailed floor plans, whether within or outside the casino premises, indicating the following (to the extent that the following relate to the specified parts of the entry levy collection system):
(i)the areas designated for the collection of entry levies;
(ii)the areas designated for entry to, or exit from, the casino premises by residents and non-residents, respectively;
(iii)a description of, and drawings which map the placement of, any electronic system comprising installations, devices or equipment that form part of the entry levy collection system;
(c)a statement by the person in charge of the casino operations that the specified parts of the entry levy collection system meet the entry levy collection requirements and comply with any direction given by the Authority in relation to the collection of entry levy and with these Regulations;
(d)such other information as the Authority may require to determine whether the specified parts of the entry levy collection system meet the entry levy collection requirements and comply with any direction given by the Authority in relation to the collection of entry levy and with these Regulations.
(2) The Authority may —
(a)approve all or any specified parts of the entry levy collection system for any casino premises subject to such conditions as the Authority may impose; or
(b)reject all or any specified parts of the entry levy collection system that do not satisfy any of the entry levy collection requirements or do not comply with any direction given by the Authority in relation to the collection of entry levy or with these Regulations.
[S 637/2026 wef 21/09/2026]
